JUnit tests can't use camera due native Matrix4.prj unloaded. Existing core tests likely have native loader? Maybe not. We can test LOD selection using fake camera overriding update and manually setting frustum planes. Frustum planes public. `Camera` is abstract with `update`, we can define TestCamera extends Camera:
```
private static class TestCamera extends Camera {
 public TestCamera(pos) {this.position.set; initFrustum();}
 @Override public void update() {}
 @Override public void update(boolean updateFrustum) {}
 void setAxes? Camera fields direction/up public final.
 void setFrustumForBox(BoundingBox region) {
  planes[0..5].set(0,0,0, d)... 
 }
}
```
To test all in frustum we can set all plane normals point inward? Plane testPoint: dot(normal,point)+d. Need all front. Easiest set each plane normal zero? Plane testPoint: if normal zero and d=0 => OnPlane not Back, so in. Is that true? Plane.testPoint simple. So set six planes normal zero d=0 => frustum includes all.
For culling, define frustum box with planes. Need planes half-space. `Plane.set(Vector3 point, Vector3 normal)` and `set(nx,ny,nz,d)` where d = -dot(normal,point). Inward. To exclude ground when camera looking up, easiest set one plane normal (0,-1,0), d= something such that y<... back. Let's just test cull with all-inclusive and one exclusion:
- `camera.includeAll()` sets planes normal 0 d0.
- `camera.includeNothing()` set plane normal (1,0,0), d = -1? `testPoint(any)` for all? Need all boxes back. Plane normal (0,1,0), d = 1e6 means y < -1e6 => back? testPoint likely dot + d <0 -> Back. Most below? y 0 => 1e6 front. Wrong. d = -1e6 => y<1e6 back. yes. Set plane0 normal (0,1,0), d=-1000 => any y<1000 is Back, excluding all. Other planes on plane. Good.
- For partial culling test could set excluding x<0? plane normal (1,0,0), d=0 => points x<0 back. But boundsInFrustum loops corners and returns false only if ALL corners Back for each plane. Left half boxes with max x<0 all back, right have some front. Set only one plane normal (1,0,0),d=0 => excludes boxes fully x<0. Great. Other planes zero. This tests partial: root all corners? min x0 max64, some not back => root passes and split; left children x0..32 some at0 front OnPlane, pass. To exclude fully x< -? none. Not partial. Set plane normal (-1,0,0), d=0 => points x>0 back, root all? min0 not back? 0 on plane not back so root passes. All children with min0 pass. Not useful.
Set plane x=-10: normal (-1,0,0), d=10 => dot=-x+10; points x>10 negative back, boxes x0..16 includes min0 front => pass. no.
To partial exclude boxes entirely at x >32, set normal (1,0,0), d=-32 => -? dot = x-32; x>32 front not back. Opposite.
Need plane normal (1,0,0), d = -? For box x<some to be Back? dot=x+d. x< -d => Back. d=-32: x<32 Back. Boxes 0..16 all back; 32.. boundary on. root some front. So excludes left chunks. Good. `plane0.set(1,0,0,-32)`. Then root passes because max64 front; left node 0..32 has max32=OnPlane, not all back? only min/max corners; max32 OnPlane so not all back => returns continue (in), but its left child 0..16 all back => excluded. So selected includes right regions but not left leaves. Good. Assert count less all and >0.
- Frustum culling uses 6 planes. all zero other. Good.
- Need no actual camera update.
